{
  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // A/B template for evaluating a default-OFF orchestration flag.
  //
  // READ THIS FIRST — the reach of `orchestrationOverride` is narrower than it
  // looks, and running an unreachable flag produces a confident NULL result that
  // means nothing. Measured against the tree at 90d527c:
  //
  //   * The overlay only affects code that reads a flag through
  //     `effectiveOrchestration()`. 45 call sites read `getConfig().orchestration`
  //     DIRECTLY and bypass it entirely — 8 of the 21 default-off orchestration
  //     flags are overlay-reachable, 13 are not.
  //   * The in-process harness invokes `runSubAgentWithStats` directly. It never
  //     reaches turn finalization, so flags read in runtime.ts / turn-*.ts cannot
  //     fire at all here regardless of the overlay.
  //
  // Intersecting those two constraints, exactly ONE default-off flag is testable
  // end-to-end with this harness today: `normalizeDelegationToEnglish`
  // (sub-agent.ts, via effectiveOrchestration). That is what the arms below use.
  //
  // The QA family (qaToolJudge, qaEvidenceRequired, deliverableConsistencyQa,
  // qaDeliveryLoopEscalateToCoordinator, resumePartialOnCorrectiveBuild,
  // maxEffortTurnOversight, reuseSessionEvidenceOnRefinement) IS overlay-reachable
  // but lives in the main-turn path. Measuring those needs the override carried
  // over the wire into the gateway process — `--via-gateway` runs elsewhere and
  // never sees this AsyncLocalStorage overlay. Not yet built.
  //
  // HOW TO RUN. The documented `pnpm agents:evaluate <plan>` does not work from
  // the repo root: `--filter` puts cwd at packages/core, so the plan path 404s and
  // the loader picks up packages/core/starlingai.json (an 8KB stub with 0
  // subAgents) instead of the real root config. Until that is fixed, invoke the
  // CLI directly from the REPO ROOT with the config and .env supplied:
  //
  //     SAI_CONFIG_PATH=<repo>/starlingai.json \
  //     SAI_PRIMARY_MODEL_URL=<your backend> SAI_LMSTUDIO_API_KEY=<key> \
  //     npx tsx packages/core/src/agent/evaluation-cli.ts \
  //         eval/flag-ab.example.jsonc out.json --repeat 5
  //
  // (The built config bakes in host.docker.internal, which no host process can
  // reach, hence the explicit URL. Relative workspacePaths resolve against cwd, so
  // the repo root matters.)
  //
  // READING THE RESULT. The arms differ only in the flag, so compare:
  //   passCount / attempts   → did it help correctness at all?
  //   cost_per_pass          → what did that cost per SUCCESSFUL run?
  //                            (add --cost-compare with a --baseline)
  //
  // Feed the two passCounts to skills/lift.ts `proportionDiffCI` and act only when
  // the interval is decisive. At k=5 a 3/5-vs-4/5 difference is well inside noise —
  // arXiv 2606.20695 finds much of the reported coordination gain in multi-agent
  // work does not clear its own noise floor. A flag that moves nothing is a delete
  // candidate, not a permanent default-off.
  //
  // SANITY CHECK BEFORE TRUSTING ANY DELTA: if the two arms report near-identical
  // token counts, the flag almost certainly did not arm. Confirm the flag is both
  // overlay-reachable and on this execution path before reading anything into the
  // pass counts.
  // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  "repeat": 5,
  "cases": [
    {
      // CONTROL — no override, byte-identical to a normal run.
      "name": "normalize-delegation--control",
      "agentName": "code_analyst",
      // No "generated/" in the task text: workspace zoning re-roots a non-`full`
      // agent (code_analyst included) INTO <workspacePath>/generated/, so cart.js
      // sits at the agent's workspace root.
      "task": "Why does cartTotal for a $50 cart with a 20% discount return a negative number instead of $40? Explain the cause. Do not edit any file.",
      "workspacePath": "eval/fixtures/assessment-trap",
      "expectIncludes": ["percent"],
      "expectNoWorkspaceChanges": true
    },
    {
      // TREATMENT — identical except the one flag under test.
      "name": "normalize-delegation--treatment",
      "agentName": "code_analyst",
      "task": "Why does cartTotal for a $50 cart with a 20% discount return a negative number instead of $40? Explain the cause. Do not edit any file.",
      "workspacePath": "eval/fixtures/assessment-trap",
      "expectIncludes": ["percent"],
      "expectNoWorkspaceChanges": true,
      "orchestrationOverride": { "normalizeDelegationToEnglish": true }
    }

    // NOTE: `userProfilePrefetch` is not worth a run at any point — its input is
    // hardwired (`const userOwnFacts = false` in agent/intent-classifier.ts), so the
    // flag cannot change behavior until that is restored.
  ]
}
